2
00:02:31.280 --> 00:02:39.890
<b>The Man Who Shook the World</b>

3
00:03:19.090 --> 00:03:20.910
Whitebeard's been...

4
00:03:21.190 --> 00:03:24.320
Whitebeard's been impaled!

5
00:03:34.510 --> 00:03:35.330
Oldtimer...

6
00:03:36.640 --> 00:03:38.650
Who's done it?!

7
00:03:38.650 --> 00:03:40.230
I think it's...

8
00:03:41.320 --> 00:03:44.880
Well, the one who attacked him was a captain from Whitebeard's alliance...

9
00:03:44.880 --> 00:03:47.210
One of the New World Pirates, Whirl Spider...

10
00:03:47.210 --> 00:03:48.910
Squardo!

11
00:03:50.220 --> 00:03:52.450
Why would you do such a thing?!

12
00:03:52.450 --> 00:03:53.810
Answer me, Squardo!

13
00:03:53.810 --> 00:03:57.580
S-Shut up! You're the ones who forced my hand!

14
00:03:57.580 --> 00:04:01.390
What?! Do you have any idea what you've-

15
00:04:04.630 --> 00:04:07.760
Old Man! If you keep pushing your body like this-

16
00:04:07.760 --> 00:04:09.040
Old Man!

17
00:04:13.440 --> 00:04:17.130
Drop the charade already, Whitebeard!

18
00:04:18.100 --> 00:04:21.090
You made a deal with the Navy, didn't you?!

19
00:04:21.090 --> 00:04:27.240
A deal to ensure that Ace and your
Whitebeard Pirates would get out of this alive!

20
00:04:28.920 --> 00:04:32.550
What's Squardo talking about?

21
00:04:32.550 --> 00:04:33.590
What's going on?!

22
00:04:33.940 --> 00:04:37.490
He's lured us all into a trap!

23
00:04:38.690 --> 00:04:41.110
I had no idea...

24
00:04:42.000 --> 00:04:47.380
But Ace is the son of Gold Roger!

25
00:04:47.950 --> 00:04:53.480
I was all alone when you found me...

26
00:04:58.520 --> 00:05:00.910
Squardo is causing a scene again!

27
00:05:04.860 --> 00:05:07.740
Is everyone here a total weakling?!

28
00:05:07.740 --> 00:05:09.950
Come at me!

29
00:05:10.440 --> 00:05:12.960
Bring me Gold Roger!

30
00:05:14.040 --> 00:05:16.750
What's wrong? You lose your nerve?!

31
00:05:17.850 --> 00:05:19.670
What's wrong, you guys?!

32
00:05:24.710 --> 00:05:27.810
I'm sure you know why I was all alone...

33
00:05:33.850 --> 00:05:37.540
It was because my cherished comrades, who I'd fought beside for so long...

34
00:05:37.540 --> 00:05:40.510
were all killed by Roger!

35
00:05:41.170 --> 00:05:46.630
I'm sure you know my hatred for Roger!

36
00:05:46.630 --> 00:05:51.730
You could have at least told me that Ace is Roger's son...

37
00:05:51.730 --> 00:05:56.140
Told me of your plans to make Ace the next Pirate King!

38
00:05:56.140 --> 00:05:58.600
Ignore the Whitebeard Pirates!

39
00:05:58.600 --> 00:06:01.040
Keep moving, pull back to the plaza!

40
00:06:01.040 --> 00:06:03.780
The oldtimer wants to make Ace the Pirate King?

41
00:06:04.250 --> 00:06:08.020
Whitebeard is the strongest pirate I know of.

42
00:06:08.020 --> 00:06:11.980
I want to make him the Pirate King.

43
00:06:17.730 --> 00:06:22.190
Even then, you had already betrayed me!

44
00:06:22.600 --> 00:06:28.170
You let me become his friend, never knowing how you were mocking me!

45
00:06:28.170 --> 00:06:33.100
And then your golden child Ace was captured!

46
00:06:33.100 --> 00:06:37.160
<b>Allied Ships</b>
<b>Human Weapons</b>

47
00:06:33.100 --> 00:06:36.190
The Whitebeard Pirates are within the bay,

48
00:06:36.190 --> 00:06:39.600
while we allied crews are out here, along the shore...

49
00:06:39.600 --> 00:06:44.680
You traded away the lives of the forty-three captains of your alliance...

50
00:06:44.680 --> 00:06:47.220
in exchange for Ace's life!

51
00:06:47.740 --> 00:06:52.620
The allied crews will be executed, while Ace and the Whitebeard Pirates are spared!

52
00:06:52.620 --> 00:06:56.230
You and Sengoku have already agreed on that, right?!

53
00:06:58.780 --> 00:07:01.950
Silence! You really expect me to believe that nonsense?!

54
00:07:09.090 --> 00:07:11.430
You still don't get it?

55
00:07:11.430 --> 00:07:14.180
You'll be eating your words soon enough.

56
00:07:14.180 --> 00:07:16.550
If you think I'm lying, just watch closely!

57
00:07:19.380 --> 00:07:25.560
The crews of the alliance will be the only targets of the attack that's about to begin!

58
00:07:26.350 --> 00:07:31.130
The Navy has agreed not to attack the Whitebeard Pirates!

59
00:07:32.070 --> 00:07:38.450
And what do you know? We came here for Ace's sake, for Whitebeard's sake...

60
00:07:38.450 --> 00:07:41.040
to lay down our lives, unaware of the deception!

61
00:07:41.040 --> 00:07:42.140
Look for yourself!

62
00:07:44.810 --> 00:07:49.050
Just as he said, we're the only ones the Navy is attacking!

63
00:07:51.120 --> 00:07:58.290
<b>Whitebeard</b>

64
00:07:51.470 --> 00:07:53.790
Those monsters are coming in from behind,

65
00:07:53.790 --> 00:07:58.310
and the left and right flanks are blocked by ice walls, meaning there's no escape!

66
00:08:00.170 --> 00:08:03.900
Old Man! Is it true?!

67
00:08:03.900 --> 00:08:06.630
Please say it's a lie, Old Man!

68
00:08:13.910 --> 00:08:16.710
It's practically a miracle that I hit you even once.

69
00:08:17.920 --> 00:08:20.160
I'm ready.

70
00:08:20.160 --> 00:08:21.150
Kill me!

71
00:08:27.550 --> 00:08:31.320
You know, we do seem to be their only targets!

72
00:08:34.700 --> 00:08:36.190
Run!

73
00:08:39.960 --> 00:08:43.800
Old Man! Did you really sell us out...

74
00:08:43.800 --> 00:08:46.440
in exchange for Ace's life?!

75
00:08:46.920 --> 00:08:49.650
Say something! Old Man!

76
00:08:50.060 --> 00:08:53.700
Old Man! Old Man!

77
00:09:09.630 --> 00:09:12.110
No way! There's gotta be some sort of mistake!

78
00:09:12.110 --> 00:09:14.210
Whitebeard making a deal with the Navy?

79
00:09:14.210 --> 00:09:15.660
Betraying his crew?

80
00:09:15.660 --> 00:09:18.000
That's unthinkable!
This is Whitebeard we're talking about!

81
00:09:18.000 --> 00:09:20.490
Whitebeard and the Navy made a deal?!

82
00:09:20.490 --> 00:09:23.660
Does this mean the pirates who trusted Whitebeard and fought alongside him...

83
00:09:23.660 --> 00:09:27.510
are betrayed and will be eliminated by the Navy?

84
00:09:27.510 --> 00:09:31.020
I didn't want to believe it... I doubted my own eyes!

85
00:09:31.020 --> 00:09:33.450
How could you betray us, Old Man?!

86
00:09:33.450 --> 00:09:35.140
You idiot!

87
00:09:35.770 --> 00:09:37.640
He was the one who took you in, Squardo!

88
00:09:37.640 --> 00:09:39.700
Why don't you have faith in the Old Man?!

89
00:09:39.700 --> 00:09:43.150
You've no right to say that, Marco!

90
00:09:43.150 --> 00:09:45.770
You're the Commander of the First Division!

91
00:09:45.770 --> 00:09:51.490
I refuse to hear you say that you didn't know... about Ace or about the deal with the Navy!

92
00:09:51.940 --> 00:09:56.830
It's true that Ace is Roger's son...

93
00:09:56.830 --> 00:10:01.650
So they found the man who'd be the most hurt to hear that, and turned him against us.

94
00:10:02.430 --> 00:10:08.210
Their plan was one step ahead of my own.

95
00:10:08.550 --> 00:10:10.700
Enough of this.

96
00:10:10.700 --> 00:10:11.390
Aokiji!

97
00:10:14.640 --> 00:10:16.360
Why is he coming here?!

98
00:10:16.850 --> 00:10:18.780
So this entire war was arranged from the beginning?!

99
00:10:18.780 --> 00:10:20.870
Then what was the point of all the fighting up to now?!

100
00:10:20.870 --> 00:10:23.160
Does this mean neither of them will win?!

101
00:10:25.190 --> 00:10:26.020
The broadcast died!

102
00:10:26.020 --> 00:10:27.060
What's going on?!

103
00:10:27.060 --> 00:10:28.210
Did it break?

104
00:10:34.380 --> 00:10:36.680
Mobilize the walls!

105
00:10:46.180 --> 00:10:52.560
That bastard... He was hit so easily, by one of his own allies!

106
00:10:53.060 --> 00:10:56.170
You're a disgrace, Whitebeard!

107
00:10:56.170 --> 00:11:01.010
I didn't know I'd lost to such a weak man!

108
00:11:05.490 --> 00:11:06.880
Croco-boy...

109
00:11:07.420 --> 00:11:08.680
Crocodile...

110
00:11:13.960 --> 00:11:20.050
Yeah, it's true... In the past , you've always been able to dodge attacks like that...

111
00:11:20.050 --> 00:11:25.360
Even injured or exhausted, or if the attack came from one of your own,

112
00:11:25.360 --> 00:11:29.370
you've never been hit by an attack like this, and that's what's bothering me!

113
00:11:31.340 --> 00:11:36.060
You want me to wear this equipment so the enemy will feel sorry for me or something?!

114
00:11:36.060 --> 00:11:36.940
Old Man!

115
00:11:36.940 --> 00:11:39.610
Your health is deteriorating.

116
00:11:53.390 --> 00:11:57.200
You realize what you've done, don't you...

117
00:11:57.200 --> 00:11:58.910
Squardo?

118
00:12:00.200 --> 00:12:04.700
You've turned your blade against your own father...

119
00:12:04.700 --> 00:12:07.840
You foolish son!

120
00:12:20.590 --> 00:12:25.090
Though you're a fool, I still love you, my son.

121
00:12:28.060 --> 00:12:32.630
Don't... try to trick me...

122
00:12:32.630 --> 00:12:36.150
You... sold out our...

123
00:12:36.150 --> 00:12:44.450
Who has dragged your pure, loyal heart into such darkness?

124
00:12:45.420 --> 00:12:49.170
A Navy insurgent.

125
00:12:50.900 --> 00:12:54.790
I'm against this plan.

126
00:12:54.790 --> 00:12:57.830
Whitebeard is the one you ought to strike down in this war.

127
00:12:57.830 --> 00:13:01.130
Going for anyone else would be a grave mistake.

128
00:13:01.130 --> 00:13:06.030
If you'll cooperate with me, I'll save the allied pirates.

129
00:13:07.540 --> 00:13:09.970
Kill Whitebeard.

130
00:13:14.990 --> 00:13:19.280
He said he'd save the allied pirates if I killed you...

131
00:13:19.980 --> 00:13:23.050
So that's what Akainu said...

132
00:13:23.050 --> 00:13:30.170
I'm painfully aware of how you hate Roger.

133
00:13:30.690 --> 00:13:32.980
But Squardo...

134
00:13:32.980 --> 00:13:37.080
It's wrong to resent a child for the sins of his father.

135
00:13:37.080 --> 00:13:39.730
What did Ace ever do to you?

136
00:13:40.300 --> 00:13:46.340
Together, you and Ace have been through pain, joy, and difficulty,

137
00:13:46.340 --> 00:13:52.150
rising above it every time, with your friends beside you.

138
00:13:52.150 --> 00:13:55.580
It doesn't matter who Ace's parents were.

139
00:13:55.580 --> 00:13:59.270
We got a chance to meet on this big, wide ocean.

140
00:13:59.270 --> 00:14:05.370
Not only you two. All of you are my sons.

141
00:14:05.370 --> 00:14:09.620
So Squardo, try to get along.

142
00:14:09.620 --> 00:14:13.540
Don't think that Ace is a special case.

143
00:14:13.540 --> 00:14:17.370
You are all my family.

144
00:14:27.080 --> 00:14:30.020
Still...

145
00:14:32.430 --> 00:14:34.670
you really...

146
00:14:37.330 --> 00:14:40.420
haven't changed, Sengoku.

147
00:14:40.420 --> 00:14:45.260
You sure duped him.

148
00:14:46.040 --> 00:14:50.400
Me, sell out my own sons' lives?!

149
00:15:03.880 --> 00:15:07.690
So he's given the pirates an escape route...

150
00:15:07.690 --> 00:15:09.190
I shouldn't have taken him so lightly.

151
00:15:14.980 --> 00:15:17.320
The wall of ice is gone...

152
00:15:17.320 --> 00:15:19.270
We can commandeer the warships!

153
00:15:19.270 --> 00:15:21.700
Now we can escape whenever we want!

154
00:15:24.400 --> 00:15:30.340
If you're pirates, then decide for yourselves what to believe!

155
00:15:39.820 --> 00:15:43.550
It was a lie after all! The Navy planned this whole thing!

156
00:15:43.550 --> 00:15:45.390
Dammit! They conned us all!

157
00:15:45.390 --> 00:15:48.900
There's no way the Old Man would betray us!

158
00:15:48.900 --> 00:15:52.430
Forgive me! I'll never doubt you again, Old Man!

159
00:15:52.430 --> 00:15:55.020
Me too, Old Man! Please forgive me!

160
00:15:55.020 --> 00:15:57.170
Old Man! I'll follow you till the end!

161
00:15:57.170 --> 00:15:58.150
Old Man!

162
00:15:58.540 --> 00:16:03.600
A weak man, you say? Give me a break, Alligator-kid!

163
00:16:03.600 --> 00:16:09.310
I'm only one man, with one heart.

164
00:16:09.310 --> 00:16:12.480
They may call me a demon or a monster or whatever,

165
00:16:12.480 --> 00:16:16.190
but I won't be the strongest forever.

166
00:16:16.190 --> 00:16:19.020
If I can help just one young life rise to the future,

167
00:16:19.020 --> 00:16:22.830
then it will be enough for me.

168
00:16:23.240 --> 00:16:27.060
Those willing to come with me, follow me even if it costs you your lives!

169
00:16:27.060 --> 00:16:35.310
Yeah!

170
00:16:38.110 --> 00:16:43.630
Attack! He's on the move! The strongest man in the world!

171
00:16:46.630 --> 00:16:48.900
Let's go!

172
00:16:48.900 --> 00:16:50.960
Yeah!

173
00:16:50.960 --> 00:16:52.860
Don't let them advance!

174
00:16:52.860 --> 00:16:54.030
Fire!

175
00:16:55.780 --> 00:16:57.460
Do as the Old Man says!

176
00:16:57.460 --> 00:16:59.300
Open a path for the Old Man!

177
00:17:21.390 --> 00:17:22.260
Whitebeard...

178
00:17:35.230 --> 00:17:37.400
Squardo...

179
00:17:37.400 --> 00:17:41.060
The Navy tricked him into going after the Old Man!

180
00:17:41.060 --> 00:17:43.510
How stupid can you get?!

181
00:17:43.770 --> 00:17:47.680
And how bad must he be feeling now?!

182
00:17:48.730 --> 00:17:51.000
But then...

183
00:17:52.810 --> 00:17:54.660
What...

184
00:17:55.760 --> 00:17:57.600
What...

185
00:18:01.070 --> 00:18:03.490
have I done?!

186
00:18:12.440 --> 00:18:14.930
I'm sorry, Old Man!

187
00:18:15.340 --> 00:18:17.880
I'm sorry, Ace!

188
00:18:26.210 --> 00:18:27.510
Squardo.

189
00:18:31.790 --> 00:18:35.350
Are you gonna cry, or are you gonna make them pay?

190
00:18:41.260 --> 00:18:44.240
That old guy sure is amazing... Even with that wound...

191
00:18:45.330 --> 00:18:48.080
But I've got to focus on Ace!

192
00:18:48.080 --> 00:18:49.440
Luffy-kun!

193
00:18:50.590 --> 00:18:51.950
Jinbei!

194
00:18:52.550 --> 00:18:54.810
Look at that!

195
00:19:15.200 --> 00:19:19.480
All our enemies have retreated to the plaza without us noticing!

196
00:19:20.390 --> 00:19:22.470
I have a bad feeling about this...

197
00:19:23.010 --> 00:19:27.280
But the Old Man has made his move!
This is no time to be second-guessing!

198
00:19:27.510 --> 00:19:31.140
Indeed! It's too late to stop now!

199
00:19:33.160 --> 00:19:34.600
Still not ready?!

200
00:19:35.320 --> 00:19:38.960
Sorry, Sir! The ice is much stronger than we anticipated.

201
00:19:51.460 --> 00:19:53.440
Charge!

202
00:19:53.780 --> 00:19:55.600
The walls should be up by now...

203
00:19:55.600 --> 00:19:56.980
This is bad!

204
00:19:56.980 --> 00:19:59.580
I'll buy us some time!

205
00:20:02.270 --> 00:20:03.310
Vice Admiral!

206
00:20:09.310 --> 00:20:13.890
I won't let you reach the plaza, Whitebeard Pirates!

207
00:20:16.830 --> 00:20:20.410
I-It's one of the Navy's Vice Admirals, John Giant!

208
00:20:29.760 --> 00:20:32.300
You're in our way.

209
00:20:56.230 --> 00:20:57.700
My balance...

210
00:20:59.680 --> 00:21:00.580
Vice-Admiral!

211
00:21:00.580 --> 00:21:02.530
Hey! The ground is tilting!

212
00:21:08.630 --> 00:21:10.580
Stay away from the Old Man!

213
00:21:11.430 --> 00:21:13.180
This isn't just an earthquake!

214
00:21:23.970 --> 00:21:25.230
The sea...

215
00:21:25.550 --> 00:21:27.430
Unbelievable...

216
00:21:27.430 --> 00:21:29.460
The whole island and the sea...

217
00:21:29.460 --> 00:21:31.670
are being tilted!

218
00:21:53.100 --> 00:21:56.430
What a crazy old geezer!

219
00:22:17.080 --> 00:22:17.940
Luffy-kun!

220
00:22:20.790 --> 00:22:22.250
Jinbei!

221
00:22:22.250 --> 00:22:24.660
I've got you now!

222
00:22:32.920 --> 00:22:34.990
You saved me... Thanks!

223
00:22:36.030 --> 00:22:37.760
You needn't thank me.

224
00:22:39.280 --> 00:22:42.460
Can't that guy tell his allies from his enemies?

225
00:22:42.460 --> 00:22:45.410
His crewmates knew to take refuge by the flanks.

226
00:22:57.610 --> 00:23:00.650
What awesome power...

227
00:23:00.650 --> 00:23:05.430
But the Navy's Absolute Justice is at stake...

228
00:23:05.430 --> 00:23:09.430
I can't let you pass!

229
00:23:29.920 --> 00:23:31.650
It's not stopping!

230
00:23:34.380 --> 00:23:36.580
It's gonna reach the execution platform!

231
00:23:36.580 --> 00:23:38.020
Go! Tear it apart!

232
00:23:51.050 --> 00:23:53.670
Hey... Is the execution platform still standing?

233
00:23:54.770 --> 00:23:56.140
Did it work?

234
00:24:01.130 --> 00:24:03.740
It didn't hit the execution platform?!

235
00:24:04.140 --> 00:24:05.950
Why did it veer off?

236
00:24:06.870 --> 00:24:08.550
T-That's...

237
00:24:10.950 --> 00:24:13.090
The Three Admirals!

238
00:24:16.820 --> 00:24:19.370
This happened because they didn't raise the walls in time.

239
00:24:19.920 --> 00:24:22.800
Because your ice is in the way!

240
00:24:24.470 --> 00:24:28.010
Why don't you just melt it, Sakazuki?

241
00:24:28.010 --> 00:24:30.810
Let's go, Whitebeard Pirates!

242
00:24:36.160 --> 00:24:38.180
Charge!

243
00:24:42.160 --> 00:24:45.550
They all seem pretty fired up...

244
00:24:45.550 --> 00:24:48.090
Scary!

245
00:24:48.670 --> 00:24:50.770
What happened to the walls?

246
00:24:50.770 --> 00:24:52.760
Sir, it's...

247
00:24:52.760 --> 00:24:55.690
I don't care if we shut down the city's whole electric grid.

248
00:24:55.690 --> 00:24:58.330
Use all the power we have to mobilize those walls!

249
00:24:58.330 --> 00:24:59.670
Yes, Sir! Right away!

250
00:25:04.250 --> 00:25:07.810
Ace!

251
00:25:14.270 --> 00:25:15.360
Luffy!

252
00:25:15.360 --> 00:25:16.190
I'm coming now!

253
00:25:18.620 --> 00:25:21.590
Ace!

254
00:25:21.590 --> 00:25:23.430
Power input, maximum!

255
00:25:34.670 --> 00:25:36.080
W-What?!

256
00:25:37.540 --> 00:25:39.280
W-Walls?!

257
00:25:45.200 --> 00:25:46.920
We're surrounded!

258
00:25:46.920 --> 00:25:48.650
What is this?!

259
00:25:52.300 --> 00:25:54.000
Dammit!

260
00:25:58.450 --> 00:25:59.640
Did I get it?

261
00:26:03.870 --> 00:26:06.090
It's hopeless! It won't budge!

262
00:26:06.090 --> 00:26:08.540
It must be incredibly dense steel!

263
00:26:08.940 --> 00:26:13.810
So the walls they were talking about earlier were these enormous defensive walls?!

264
00:26:13.810 --> 00:26:16.550
Dammit! So you're not gonna fight us then, Navy?!

265
00:26:20.430 --> 00:26:22.280
Hey, look at that!

266
00:26:22.280 --> 00:26:25.260
All the cannons are pointed at us!

267
00:26:25.260 --> 00:26:27.090
Let's run away!

268
00:26:27.090 --> 00:26:30.040
We're surrounded! Where are we supposed to...

269
00:26:33.680 --> 00:26:34.910
There's an opening!

270
00:26:34.910 --> 00:26:37.000
Hey! What's going on?!

271
00:26:37.000 --> 00:26:38.580
Raise all of the walls!

272
00:26:38.950 --> 00:26:44.350
Well... The walls can't handle the massive weight of Oars' body!

273
00:26:44.730 --> 00:26:49.750
And it looks like his blood leaked into the system and damaged it!

274
00:26:51.830 --> 00:26:53.330
Seriously? Damn demon!

275
00:26:54.800 --> 00:26:57.760
Oars... You...

276
00:27:01.600 --> 00:27:03.990
What an incredible guy!

277
00:27:05.460 --> 00:27:09.550
He's still fighting... even now.

278
00:27:14.350 --> 00:27:16.410
Admirable!

279
00:27:17.690 --> 00:27:19.220
They may not be closed in...

280
00:27:19.810 --> 00:27:21.850
but proceed with the operation, Akainu!

281
00:27:44.130 --> 00:27:46.020
Meteor Volcano!

282
00:28:00.570 --> 00:28:01.990
What's going on?!

283
00:28:05.140 --> 00:28:06.890
We're not letting you escape!

284
00:28:07.480 --> 00:28:10.630
Melt the ice and take away their footing!

